+Five racing models near 10,000 triangles — 2026-11-14
+
+The owner's revised target is approximately 10,000 triangles. **Rally, Kart, Forklift, Volt and Hover now have 9,987–10,504 stock master triangles.** Challenger is excluded at the owner's request because its model is still being developed. No Challenger budget resources were published or Challenger prepared models rebuilt by this pass.
+
+| Stock racing model | Previous master | New master | Reduction | Active unique mesh bytes before → after |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Rally | 19,074 | 10,294 | 46.03% | 719,308 → 461,234 |
+| Kart | 24,223 | 10,294 | 57.50% | 1,274,442 → 853,908 |
+| Forklift | 26,472 | 10,504 | 60.32% | 1,259,444 → 652,202 |
+| Volt | 19,826 | 9,987 | 49.63% | 600,872 → 345,892 |
+| Hover | 22,068 | 10,300 | 53.33% | 606,820 → 314,394 |
+
+Across these five catalogue masters: **111,663 → 51,379 triangles (−53.99%)**. This sum is not a single race frame. The buffer column includes active unique geometry/index/LOD/morph/shadow payloads, not total process RAM or VRAM. Existing textures, including the printed Rally plate, are unchanged.
+
+The target applies to stock **simple/racing** models. The sampled four-category equipped builds are Rally **12,254**, Kart **10,384**, Forklift **12,064**, Volt **10,504** and Hover **11,649** triangles. Optional kits can exceed 10,000; this is not a hard cap on every combination. Full-quality stock masters retain **102,556 / 72,544 / 148,048 / 114,648 / 71,932** triangles and exactly the same measured prepared buffer totals as the task-start references. No driving tune, collision source, replay source, car configuration or ghost implementation was authored.
+
+**C10K01 — Offline geometry and allocation.** The new `game/vehicle/car_budget_reduction.gd` loads immutable source-keyed mesh resources. It runs after sibling batching, allowing useful reductions across previously tiny pieces, and before transform-frame batching. There is no runtime decimator. Missing resources, changed source geometry, wrong source metadata, material-slot mismatch or changed bounds retain the original mesh. Its mesh cache is bounded to 256 entries. Challenger exits before lookup.
+
+Most pieces use offline Blender limited dissolve and retessellation. Original source-corner IDs survive the operations; the Godot packer selects those original encoded vertex records. Positions, normals, UVs and other retained attributes therefore remain exact source values, while connectivity and interpolation change. Mirror regions restore components that would disappear or lose their bounds. Rally's stock bonnet keeps its original topology. Kart uses the existing native index candidates for static geometry; its three steering meshes and all ten moving-driver poses remain protected. Boundary simplification on eligible Kart/Forklift pieces is an explicit lower-detail choice. These operations do not establish a maximum surface-distance error.
+
+The offline pipeline is `game/tests/bake_car_10k.gd`, `export_car_10k_surfaces.gd`, `export_car_10k_roles.gd` and `scripts/dissolve_car_10k.py`. Blender **4.5.15 LTS** runs with factory startup and auto-execution disabled, consumes exported arrays, and never opens or saves an owner Blender project. The published set contains **710 resources** for the five included IDs. Source-key/encoded-attribute checks exercise 1,673 real changed-part observations across stock and all offered replacements.
+
+**C10K02 — Consistent assemblies and finishes.** Simple source construction retains editable part boundaries through the shared reduction, then merges fixed stock frames and installs their existing stock shadow proxies before final batching. Source-fitted construction follows the same independent module path. All five stock and sampled fitted cases retain their previous visible surface counts: stock **52 / 46 / 26 / 38 / 19**, sampled fitted **68 / 65 / 40 / 40 / 47**. Paint, sticker bindings, lights, steering nodes and wheel transforms remain live. These counts describe material surfaces, not measured total draw calls.
+
+**C10K03 — Appearance and performance tradeoff.** This density has a visible cost. Tyres, helmets, wheel arches, body highlights and small fittings are more angular. Some close details and the translucent ghost's internal lines are simpler. The comparison images are the review evidence; this is not an appearance-identity claim. In exchange, near/master geometry is about 46–60% smaller for the included stock cars, and active mesh buffers are smaller. Pixel/shader work, CPU submission, track geometry and shadow work remain separate costs, so this does not imply the same percentage FPS gain.
+
+[Mobile comparison sheet](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/mobile-comparison.png) · [Compatibility comparison sheet](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/gl_compatibility-comparison.png). Before is left, approximately 10k is right. All 74 full native pairs and their control statistics are represented in [pixel metrics](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/native-pixel-metrics.json). The sheets show representative views; full stock/fitted front, rear and distance captures are alongside them.
+
+There are **37 pairs per renderer**: 30 opaque stock/fitted views, two close plate views and five ghosts. All 32 opaque/plate pairs per renderer have exact repeat/restoration controls. Compatibility completes **163 checks / two failures**, both unchanged Rally ghost reference/restoration controls: eight/six pixels differ by at most **1/255 RGB**, with no changed alpha pixels. Desktop Mobile completes **163/0**. Those Compatibility controls remain a qualification failure; their tiny noise does not explain away the actual, much larger candidate ghost differences.
+
+The worst opaque crop mean is **8.3945/255 Compatibility** and **5.7805/255 Mobile**; at most **21.7145% / 21.3727%** of crop pixels change by more than eight RGB levels. Ghost crop means reach **5.3136/255 / 4.2652/255**, with up to **18.9589% / 17.9878%** of pixels over eight. These are measured appearance differences without an invented acceptance threshold. Owner appearance acceptance remains open.
+
+At the distance camera, actual prepared whole-scene visible-primitive counters fall as follows in both renderers:
+
+| Car | Before | After | Reduction |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Rally | 22,324 | 14,336 | 35.78% |
+| Kart | 26,439 | 14,302 | 45.91% |
+| Forklift | 28,974 | 14,034 | 51.56% |
+| Volt | 22,588 | 13,765 | 39.06% |
+| Hover | 22,818 | 14,124 | 38.10% |
+
+These counters include the studio and its passes. Existing LODs explain why savings differ from master counts. They are not an actual race frame-time benchmark. No physical-device query/test, APK/export or device FPS measurement was performed.
+
+**C10K04 — Consumers and qualification.** Five full/simple bases, all five cars' full/simple kit sets, five full-quality Garage references, the stock header and five catalogue photographs were refreshed. Challenger's picture and its prior per-car provenance were retained; global Challenger readiness is deliberately unqualified. The scoped photograph validator passes **five images / 173 current source hashes**. The consumed-source fence covers **24,524 unchanged inputs**, and strict prepared validation passes **468 resources / 1,925 checks / zero failures**, explicitly excluding Challenger.
+
+| Actual verification | Checks / failures |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Encoded source attributes, slots, bounds, fixed/editable budgets and all source replacements | 6,748 / 0 |
+| Actual prepared stock/fitted/full hits and budgets | 50 / 0 |
+| Existing all-kit source/prepared/material/ghost comparisons, five cars and both tiers | 7,545 / 0 |
+| Actual Garage/race App, each desktop renderer | 48 / 0 |
+| Header appearance and actual prepared delivery, each renderer | 496 / 0 |
+| Prepared native Kart steering, pose independence and grip checks | 170 / 0 |
+| Five-car washing / Garage surface regression | 1,383 / 0 and 54 / 0 |
+| Driving / production parsing | 72 / 0 and 573 / 0 |
+
+The App Mobile first run passes its 48 assertions but reports the known two-object/one-resource teardown diagnostic; its repeat exits cleanly. This is not a teardown-fix claim. Two headless Forklift kit producers report `material_get_instance_shader_parameters` with a null material during final cleanup. The accepted Forklift producer and exhaustive module suite run in native Compatibility and exit cleanly, with 104 produced modules and 1,726 successful comparisons. The headless findings remain in the receipts, rather than being suppressed or reported as clean runs.
+
+Earlier attempts exposed lost mirrors, source/component pruning, overconservative component floors, unsuitable coarse joining skins, a staging-directory/bounds issue and a scoped-washing fixture that still expected six cars. They were rejected or corrected. A concurrent Challenger native refresh invalidated its cached candidates; the owner subsequently excluded it. Rejected candidates remained private. The exact-bound check was corrected to compare the actual source mesh rather than a temporary conversion's reconstructed bounds. Existing production/module assertions were retained. The five-car washing fixture now checks the exact five expected condition keys and still rejects PB writes. The known pre-existing Hover source-only stock-reset variation remains explicit; prepared replacement parity is covered by the unchanged module suite.
+
+Commands actually run are recorded individually with full engine arguments, exit codes and diagnostics. Representative successful invocations from the root:
+
+```powershell
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py export-dissolve res://tests/export_car_10k_surfaces.gd --headless
+# Blender executable: build/tools/blender-4.5.15-windows-x64/blender.exe
+# --background --factory-startup --disable-autoexec --python-exit-code 1
+# --python scripts/dissolve_car_10k.py; repeated with -- --boundaries
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py protected-roles res://tests/export_car_10k_roles.gd --headless
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py stage-final-five res://tests/bake_car_10k.gd --headless -- --resume --replan --dissolved --boundaries
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py source-final res://tests/test_car_10k.gd --headless
+python scripts/refresh_car_10k_assets.py --finish
+python scripts/refresh_car_10k_assets.py --pictures
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py kits-forklift-native res://tests/bake_modular_car_kits.gd --rendering-method gl_compatibility -- --vehicle=forklift
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py prepared-results res://tests/measure_car_10k_results.gd --headless -- --prepared
+# Existing module suite run for all five IDs; Forklift uses native Compatibility:
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py modules-compact res://tests/test_modular_car_assets.gd --headless -- --vehicle=compact --all-kits
+# Native captures/App/icons run in gl_compatibility and mobile:
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py native-final-gl res://tests/capture_car_10k_models.gd --rendering-method gl_compatibility
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py app-gl res://tests/test_car_10k_app.gd --rendering-method gl_compatibility
+python scripts/run_car_10k.py steering res://tests/test_car_10k_steering.gd --rendering-method gl_compatibility -- --prepared
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/compare_car_10k.ps1
+```
+
+The initial refresh ran base/kit stages before the headless Forklift cleanup diagnostic stopped its wrapper. `--finish` completed the remaining consumers using the original qualified five-car source fence. Native Forklift production qualified the final kit files. `scripts/bake_car_10k.py` now documents the complete collect/export/Blender/protect/pack/proof workflow and optional explicit publication; its Python syntax was checked, while the qualified execution above used those underlying commands individually. The isolated runner redirects APPDATA/LOCALAPPDATA, disables API configuration and uses Dummy audio.
+
+Production source edits are `car_visual.gd`, `racing_car_models.gd`, `prepared_asset_dependencies.json` and the new `car_budget_reduction.gd`; native five-car derivatives and prepared consumers accompany them. Build identity/project metadata are generated by the existing helper. No main-index staging/commit, backend request/deployment or owner-save/process change was performed. A fresh client launch, owner appearance review and device performance acceptance remain separate.
+
+Closeout controls, generated-file hashes, source checkpoint and retention results are recorded in the adjoining task evidence directory.
+
+The [final control receipt](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/final-controls.json) confirms unchanged ghost/handling sources and eight car configurations, with concurrent index changes preserved. [Generated asset hashes](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/final-assets.json), [module results](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/module-results.json), [source-only patch](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/source.patch) and [byte-exact private-checkpoint receipt](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/source-checkpoint.json) make the result reviewable. The checkpoint stages only a small private repository under disposable build output.
+
+Task-owned intermediate geometry/JSON caches totalling 130,009,079 bytes were removed, and obsolete Challenger draft pictures were moved into disposable output. The mandatory `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/clean_build.ps1 -Apply` completed; its actual remaining size and protected/recent exclusions are recorded in the [retention log](evidence/car-10k-models-2026-11-14/build-retention.log). No historical pins or owner processes were removed.
